  "question": {
    "text": "A class contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;boys and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> girls. If the number of ways of selecting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> boys and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> girls from the class is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>168</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>g</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "17",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mtext>&#160;boys&#160;and&#160;g&#160;girls</mtext></math></p><p>Also given total ways of selecting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mtext>&#160;boys&#160;and&#160;2&#160;girls</mtext></math>&nbsp;which will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>b</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#215;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>g</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>168</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>168</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now on comparing both side we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
